   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter">
                <dateline>
                    <name type="geo" key="G_CHE_LOCA">Locarno</name>
                    <lb/>
                    <date when="1917-11-05">5/XI/17</date>  <seg xml:id="seg1" type="note-anchor">--1</seg>
                </dateline>
                <div type="address">
                    <ab>
                        <address>
                            <addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="G_CHE_LOCA_02">Pension Daheim</name>
                            </addrLine>
                            <addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="G_CHE_LOCA">Locarno</name>
                            </addrLine>
                        </address>
                    </ab>
                </div>
                <div type="mainBody">
                    <p>Dear <name type="person" key="syke83">Mr. Sykes</name>: This is a new address. I send you back <seg xml:id="seg2" type="note-anchor">
                            <hi rend="underline">Irish Blather</hi>
                        </seg> which I have read. Many thanks. If possible I should like to see other numbers, old or new. I <choice>
                            <sic>suuppose</sic>
                            <corr>suppose</corr>
                        </choice> the Fortnightly has not yet arrived. Weather good here. Two dull days since we came. For the rest, sun. <rs type="person" key="barn84">My wife</rs> got <name type="person" key="race85">Mrs. <choice>
                                <sic>Syke’s</sic>
                                <corr>Sykes’s</corr>
                            </choice>
                        </name> kind letter and will write – very soon. Am getting on with <rs type="work" key="W_ULYSSES">my book</rs>.</p>
                    <closer>
                        <salute>Kind regards from us all to Mrs. Sykes and yourself.</salute>
                        <signed>
                            <name type="person" key="joyc82">James Joyce</name>.</signed>
                    </closer>
                </div>
            </div> <div type="notes">
                <note xml:id="note1" target="#seg1" type="commentary">The original of this item was transcribed by Claud Sykes for Herbert Gorman. See Steven Lund, <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">James Joyce: Letters, Manuscripts, and Photographs at Southern Illinois University</name> (Troy: Whitston, 1983), 11. Typographical oddities have been retained.</note> <note xml:id="note2" target="#seg2" type="commentary">Joyce is returning the <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">Irische Blätter</name>, the newsletter of the Deutsch-Irische Gesellschaft, from which he copied material for <name type="work" key="W_ULYSSES">Ulysses</name>.</note>
            </div>
      </body>
   </text>
